@startuml selma_authorization
' ============================================================
' Selma — Capability Authorization State Machine
' Source:  SPECIFICATION.md §3.2, §3.2.1, §9.6
'          User_Stories.md S-32, S-33, S-34
' C4:      Application Service (ingress gate)
'          + Lifecycle Finder / Conflict Resolver (domain gates)
'          denials → Findings & Audit Trail Adapter → event_store
' Contract: 8.2.4
'
' Cross-cutting behavioral security model. Applies to humans,
' service accounts, and AI agents (same matrix; actor = agent ID).
' Delegation is NOT supported in v8.2.x.
' ============================================================

title Selma — Capability Authorization FSM\n<size:12><i>Request → matrix → SoD → stage gate → allow | deny + audit · hard-reject semantics</i></size>

!include ./common/sm_styles.puml

[*] --> RequestReceived : any mutating or gated read

state "Request\nReceived" as RequestReceived #B9770E : raw request at interface
state "Identity\nVerified" as IdentityVerified #1B7A6E : authenticated actor\nrole bound (RO | CR | System | AI)
state "Capability\nEvaluated" as CapabilityEvaluated #1B7A6E : matrix lookup\nrole × capability
state "SoD\nEvaluated" as SoDEvaluated #B9770E : only when action is\nfinding.waive or\nfinding.approve_remediation
state "Stage Gate\nChecked" as StageGateChecked #1B7A6E : enforcement point match
state "Allowed" as Allowed #2C6E49 : proceed to domain FSM\nor pipeline
state "Denied" as Denied #A93226 : 403 CapabilityDenied
state "Denial\nAudited" as DenialAudited #4A4A4A : append-only denial record
state "Domain State\nUnchanged" as DomainUnchanged #A93226 : no mutation\nno compensating event

RequestReceived --> IdentityVerified : authenticate
RequestReceived --> Denied : unauthenticated

IdentityVerified --> CapabilityEvaluated : role resolved
CapabilityEvaluated --> SoDEvaluated : matrix PASS\n(and SoD-relevant action)
CapabilityEvaluated --> StageGateChecked : matrix PASS\n(non-SoD action)
CapabilityEvaluated --> Denied : matrix FAIL\ncapability not granted to role

SoDEvaluated --> StageGateChecked : SoD PASS
SoDEvaluated --> Denied : SoD FAIL\ncreator_provenance or\nevidence_submitter conflict

StageGateChecked --> Allowed : stage capability OK
StageGateChecked --> Denied : stage capability FAIL

Allowed --> [*] : dispatch domain command
Denied --> DenialAudited : record\n{actor, capability, action,\noutcome:denied, timestamp, reason}
DenialAudited --> DomainUnchanged
DomainUnchanged --> [*]

note right of CapabilityEvaluated
  **Capability matrix (§3.2) — summary**
  Official: directive.* · finding.dismiss/waive/
    approve/reject/supersede · conflict.resolve · views
  Compliance: inspection.submit/reinspect ·
    finding.acknowledge · evidence.submit · views
  System: inspection.submit · finding.view · analytics.view
  AI agents: same matrix; actor = agent ID
end note

note left of SoDEvaluated
  **SoD algorithm (§3.2.1)**
  finding.waive:
    DENY if actor ∈ creator_provenance(control_id)
  finding.approve_remediation:
    DENY if actor == evidence_submitter(finding_id)
  All other actions: SoD N/A → skip to stage gate
end note

note bottom of Denied
  **Uniform failure semantics**
  · Hard reject — no partial writes
  · No compensating success events
  · No degraded-mode execution
  · No automatic escalation
  · Caller receives error; decides next action
end note

note right of StageGateChecked
  **Five enforcement points**
  1. Request ingress (Application Service)
  2. Directive mutations (before write lock)
  3. Inspection pipeline entry
  4. Finding FSM transitions
  5. Conflict resolution
end note

@enduml
